❯ # Build the Lunchtime Jobs Claude Code Development        
  Toolkit                                                   
                                                            
  I want you to turn this repository into a well-organized  
  Minecraft mod development workspace.                      
                                                            
  You are not being asked to implement another profession   
  yet. Your task is to improve the development environment, 
  project knowledge, reusable workflows and                 
  quality-control systems so future development is more     
  reliable.                                                 
                                                            
  ## 1. Understand the existing project first               
                                                            
  Inspect:                                                  
                                                            
  - Existing Java source code.                              
  - Gradle configuration and dependencies.                  
  - Forge version and Minecraft version.                    
  - Existing professions and their implementations.         
  - Networking and capability architecture.                 
  - Unit tests and GameTests.                               
  - Current CLAUDE.md and documentation.                    
  - Git status and recent commits.                          
  - Existing mod compatibility implementations.             
                                                            
  Our environment is:                                       
                                                            
  - Minecraft 1.20.1                                        
  - Forge 47.4.28                                           
  - Java 17                                                 
  - Mod ID: lunchtimejobs                                   
  - Package: com.lunchtime.jobs                             
                                                            
  Preserve the existing implementation and all working      
  functionality.                                            
                                                            
  ## 2. Organize project knowledge                          
                                                            
  Create or improve a documentation structure covering:     
                                                            
  - Overall architecture.                                   
  - Profession architecture and activity definitions.       
  - XP engine and progression.                              
  - Networking and multiplayer synchronization.             
  - Player capability lifecycle.                            
  - Anti-exploit rules.                                     
  - Testing and GameTests.                                  
  - Mod compatibility.                                      
  - Architecture decisions.                                 
                                                            
  Keep CLAUDE.md concise, ideally below 200 lines.          
                                                            
  Move specialized instructions into appropriately scoped   
  .claude/rules files and technical knowledge into          
  documentation.                                            
                                                            
  Do not automatically load every large documentation file  
  into every session.                                       
                                                            
  ## 3. Create reusable Claude Code skills                  
                                                            
  Create the following project skills under                 
  `.claude/skills/`:                                        
                                                            
  ### new-profession                                        
                                                            
  A workflow for designing a profession before              
  implementation.                                           
                                                            
  It must define:                                           
                                                            
  - Profession identity.                                    
  - Activities.                                             
  - XP sources and values.                                  
  - Required Forge events.                                  
  - Player attribution.                                     
  - Successful-action verification.                         
  - Anti-exploit protections.                               
  - Mod compatibility.                                      
  - Performance impact.                                     
  - Unit tests and GameTests.                               
                                                            
  It must produce an implementation plan before editing     
  Java files.                                               
                                                            
  ### mod-compat-audit                                      
                                                            
  Investigates compatibility with a particular Minecraft    
  mod.                                                      
                                                            
  It must inspect actual source code, installed JARs or     
  decompiled classes where available.                       
                                                            
  It must identify:                                         
                                                            
  - Exact mod version.                                      
  - Relevant classes and methods.                           
  - Events and callbacks.                                   
  - Player attribution.                                     
  - Cancellation behavior.                                  
  - Automation behavior.                                    
  - Optional integration requirements.                      
  - Testing requirements.                                   
                                                            
  Never claim an integration works without evidence.        
                                                            
  ### forge-event-research                                  
                                                            
  Investigates Minecraft Forge 1.20.1 event behavior.       
                                                            
  It should trace the actual execution flow of an activity  
  instead of assuming that a particular event represents a  
  successful action.                                        
                                                            
  ### xp-exploit-audit                                      
                                                            
  Reviews profession implementations for:                   
                                                            
  - Duplicate XP.                                           
  - Automation exploits.                                    
  - FakePlayers.                                            
  - Creative and Spectator abuse.                           
  - Repeated interactions.                                  
  - Player attribution problems.                            
  - Multiplayer race conditions.                            
  - Memory leaks.                                           
  - Performance issues.                                     
                                                            
  It should be read-only and report findings rather than    
  automatically rewriting code.                             
                                                            
  ### verify-mod                                            
                                                            
  Create a repeatable verification workflow for this        
  project.                                                  
                                                            
  It should know how to run:                                
                                                            
  - ./gradlew clean test build                              
  - ./gradlew runGameTestServer                             
                                                            
  It must report each verification level separately.        
                                                            
  Never describe compilation as gameplay verification.      
                                                            
  ### release-check                                         
                                                            
  Reviews the final implementation, dependencies,           
  compatibility, configuration, tests, Git diff and         
  changelog before a milestone is considered complete.      
                                                            
  ## 4. Create specialist subagents                         
                                                            
  Create project-specific subagents under                   
  `.claude/agents/`.                                        
                                                            
  ### forge-architect                                       
                                                            
  Specialist in Minecraft 1.20.1 Forge mod architecture,    
  Java 17, events, registries, capabilities, networking,    
  lifecycle and dedicated-server compatibility.             
                                                            
  ### mod-compatibility-researcher                          
                                                            
  Specialist in investigating other Minecraft mods, public  
  APIs, source code, JARs, event sequences and optional     
  integrations.                                             
                                                            
  Read-only by default.                                     
                                                            
  ### multiplayer-exploit-auditor                           
                                                            
  Specialist in detecting XP abuse, event duplication,      
  automation exploits, player attribution problems and      
  multiplayer bugs.                                         
                                                            
  Read-only by default.                                     
                                                            
  ### testing-engineer                                      
                                                            
  Specialist in unit testing, Forge GameTests, regression   
  testing, Gradle builds and dedicated-server verification. 
                                                            
  Give agents only the tools and permissions they need.     
                                                            
  Use separate context for research-heavy tasks so the      
  primary implementation conversation stays focused.        
                                                            
  Consider project-scoped persistent memory for specialist  
  agents where it is useful.                                
                                                            
