  ⎿  Created 0001-server-authoritative-single-entry-point.md (+9 -0)
      1 +# ADR-0001: Server-authoritative progression with one XP entry point
      2 +                                                                    
      3 +Status: Accepted (reconstructed) · Milestones 1–2                   
      4 +                                                                    
      5 +**Context.** Multiplayer servers must not trust clients, and many ha
        +ndlers award XP.                                                    
      6 +**Decision.** All XP flows through `ProfessionService.awardXp`, whic
        +h rejects the client side, unknown/locked/inactive                  
      7 +professions and max level, applies multipliers, fires `ProfessionXpE
        +vent.Pre/Post` and `ProfessionLevelUpEvent`,                        
      8 +and syncs the client. Clients only receive S→C packets.             
      9 +**Consequences.** Handlers stay thin. Other mods can observe or canc
        +el XP through events. Every award costs a sync packet (see W-N1).   
  ⎿  Created 0002-deferred-next-tick-verification.md (+10 -0)
       1 +# ADR-0002: Deferred next-tick verification for pre-success events 
       2 +                                                                   
       3 +Status: Accepted (reconstructed) · Milestones 3, 4                 
       4 +                                                                   
       5 +**Context.** `BlockEvent.BreakEvent`, `RightClickBlock` and `Entity
         +Interact` fire *before* the outcome, and the                       
       6 +action can still fail or be canceled by another mod.               
       7 +**Decision.** Capture the pre-state, enqueue (capped at 2048, 40-ti
         +ck expiry, keyed by dimension + target + activity),                
       8 +and at `ServerTickEvent` END on a later tick compare the post-state
         + and re-resolve the player by UUID. Award only on a verified change
         +.                                                                  
       9 +**Consequences.** One tick of latency. Keys without the player let 
         +concurrent actors overwrite each other (W-F1).                     
      10 +Verification predicates must be strict (see W-R1, W-R2).           
  ⎿  Created 0003-deny-automation-and-non-survival.md (+8 -0)
      1 +# ADR-0003: FakePlayers, creative and spectator earn no XP by defaul
        +t                                                                   
      2 +                                                                    
      3 +Status: Accepted (reconstructed) · Milestones 3–5                   
      4 +                                                                    
      5 +**Decision.** Every handler rejects creative and spectator. `FakePla
        +yer` instances are rejected unless                                  
      6 +`farmer.allowFakePlayerXp` is true. That key lives in the `[farmer]`
        + config section but is read by all three professions.               
      7 +**Consequences.** Create deployers and similar automation are expect
        +ed to earn nothing (unverified per mod). The                        
      8 +config key's section name is misleading. Moving it would change the 
        +config file, so it needs a migration decision.                      
  ⎿  Created 0004-exclude-replaceable-crops.md (+8 -0)
      1 +# ADR-0004: Melon, pumpkin, sugar cane and cactus excluded from Farm
        +er                                                                  
      2 +                                                                    
      3 +Status: Accepted (reconstructed) · Milestone 3.1                    
      4 +                                                                    
      5 +**Context.** These blocks can be placed by the player in a harvest-r
        +eady state, which makes infinite place-and-break XP possible.       
      6 +**Decision.** Their adapters (`STEM_PRODUCE`, `TALL_CROPS`) match no
        +thing. The registry comment says they stay excluded "until          
      7 +persistent block placement tracking is implemented".                
      8 +**Consequences.** Legitimate gourd and cane farming earns nothing. R
        +e-enabling requires placement tracking plus tests.                  
  ⎿  Created 0005-per-profession-multiplier-replaces-global.md (+10 -0)
       1 +# ADR-0005: Per-profession multiplier replaces the global multiplie
         +r                                                                  
         +ilestone 2                                                         
       4 +                                                                   
       5 +**Observed behavior.** `ModConfig.getProfessionMultiplier`: if `per
         +ProfessionXpMultipliers` has `id=value`, the result                
       6 +is `value`. Otherwise it is `globalXpMultiplier`. They are not mult
         +iplied.                                                            
       7 +**Ambiguity.** The method Javadoc says "taking into account global 
         +multiplier and per-profession overrides".                          
       8 +A server owner may expect `global × per-profession`.               
       9 +**Decision needed.** Keep replace semantics (document them in the c
         +onfig comment) or switch to multiplicative.                        
      10 +Either change alters XP, so it requires explicit approval, a CHANGE
         +LOG entry and test updates.                                        
  ⎿  … 3 more files changed
  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode

