  Two findings that matter more than the toolkit

  - The canonical pack already has a profession system. Its KubeJS scripts
    (lunchtime_careers.js and nine *_skills.js files) give Pufferfish's Skills XP
    for farming, chef, rancher and six other careers, using the same block, craft,
    smelt and interact actions Lunchtime Jobs rewards. Installed side by side, one
    harvest would give XP in both systems. You'll need to decide whether Lunchtime
    Jobs replaces, coexists with, or bridges to it. I wrote this up in
    docs/compatibility/mods/kubejs-lunchtime-careers.md.
  - Two right-click-harvest mods are active. RightClickHarvest has radius harvest
    on, and Quark's Simple Harvest is enabled, including harvesting by villagers.
    These come first in the compatibility research queue for Farmer.

  I also corrected things from my first overview. JobsPlus, FastWorkbench,
  FastFurnace, Connector, FTB Quests and Goblin Traders were in instance (1) only
  and aren't in (2). The real GameTest count is 44, not 47; my earlier count
  included the three class-level @GameTestHolder annotations.

