  Path: docs/decisions/
  Purpose: 7 short decision records (0001–0007); 0005 is an open question for you

  New facts the docs now record:
  - The Rancher handler hard-codes vanilla animals and items for milking and
    shearing. Registering a modded animal with the registry has no XP effect.
  - unlockedByDefault is set on every profession but never read.
  - Alex's Mobs is in the mods folder but didn't load in the last launch. It looks
    like it was moved in after that launch.

  Safeguards

  .claude/settings.json:
  - Blocked: git push, reset --hard, clean, rebase, commit --amend, branch -D,
    checkout --, filter-branch, rm -rf.
  - Asks you first: commit, tag, merge, cherry-pick, stash, and edits to
    build.gradle, settings.gradle, gradle.properties, the Gradle wrapper, mods.toml,
    .claude/settings.json and the hooks.
  - Allowed without asking: git status, git diff, git log, git show, and the verify
    script.
  - Bypass mode: disabled.
  
  guard_bash.py (checks every shell command, including chained ones):
  - Blocks push and destructive git commands, even inside chains like x && git push.
  - Blocks recursive deletes outside build/, run/, logs/ and temp folders.
  - Blocks deleting or moving test files from the shell. 
  - Blocks shell edits to build files (sed -i, >>, tee).
  
  guard_edits.py (checks every file edit):
  - Asks you before any edit that removes a test or adds @Disabled.
  - Keeps the three read-only agents inside their own memory folders. Enabling
    memory on an agent automatically gives it Write and Edit, so this hook is what
    keeps them read-only.
  - Keeps testing-engineer to src/test/** and the GameTest package.
  
  No MCP servers, plugins or tools were installed.

  Limitations

  - Hooks in agents tested with fake inputs only. The per-agent rules depend on
    Claude Code passing the agent name to hooks (documented behaviour), but I
    haven't seen them fire inside a real agent run. The forked skills haven't run
    end to end either.
  - The shell guard is pattern-based. A script that deletes files itself (e.g.
    python -c) gets past it. The permission rules are the backstop; only sandboxing
    would fully enforce it.
  - No mod has been researched at source level yet. Every matrix entry is Planned,
    except KubeJS (Investigating). Lunchtime Jobs isn't in the pack and no other
    mods are in the dev setup, so modded GameTests aren't possible yet.
  - The inventory's load status is stale and incomplete:
    - It comes from the launch log of Oct 30, 22:27. 11 JARs changed after that.
    - 8 JARs have no mod ID the parser can read, mostly structure packs that use an
      inline-table mods.toml format.
  - Small fixes I applied during the work:
    - Edit rules use root-anchored paths after the docs check.
    - I replaced my first edit hook with a better one. The old one was briefly live
      and blocked one of my writes until I fixed the settings.
  - README.md is still out of date. I didn't edit it because it's tracked;
    docs/architecture/overview.md is the accurate version.
  - verify.sh is macOS-specific: it finds Java 17 with /usr/libexec/java_home. Set
    JAVA17_HOME to use it elsewhere.
  - Agent memory is shared through git: .claude/agent-memory/ will be committed when
    you commit, by design.

  Decisions for you

  1. How Lunchtime Jobs should coexist with the pack's KubeJS careers.
  2. Decision record 0005: should a per-profession XP multiplier replace the global
     multiplier (current behaviour) or multiply it?
  3. Whether to run /xp-exploit-audit on the three professions to confirm or rule
     out the eight possible weaknesses in docs/anti-exploit.md.

