     explicit approval and cannot be auto-allowed by permission rules.

     This check does not fire on a target that cannot expand to the filesystem root:
     rewrite it as `"${d:?}"/*.pyc`, which makes the shell stop with an error
     instead of running rm when $d is unset or empty, or use a literal absolute
     path.

